The market is currently pricing a middle scenario: continued disruption at moderate intensity, with no full resolution and no major infrastructure escalation. The two tail risks are a strike on Gulf energy facilities, which would spike prices sharply higher, and a new ceasefire agreement, which J.P. Morgan projects could return WTI toward $60.<br><br>
